=======================
Automation Mojo Errors
=======================

The ``automojo-errors`` package is the shared exception and traceback vocabulary for the automojo suite. It centralises the special-purpose exception types that the coding standards single out — most notably ``ConfigurationError``, ``SemanticError``, and ``CommandError`` — along with a collection of other reusable exception classes (for example ``AbstractMethodError``, ``CancelledError``) that prevent downstream packages from inventing their own near-duplicates.

Highlights
==========

- Curated exception hierarchy with ``ConfigurationError``, ``SemanticError``, ``CommandError``, ``AbstractMethodError``, and ``CancelledError``.
- Enhanced-traceback support in ``xtraceback.py`` with ``TRACEBACK_CONFIG`` and ``VALID_MEMBER_TRACE_POLICY`` knobs.
- ``raising.py`` helper module for building rich, contextual errors in the multi-line style prescribed by the coding standards.
- Dependency-light design that sits near the bottom of the automojo graph and is imported by virtually every other ``automojo-*`` package.

Repository Structure
====================

- ``development/`` - Runtime environment scripts.
- ``repository-setup/`` - Repository homing and setup scripts.
- ``source/packages/`` - Package source code.
- ``source/tests/`` - ``unittest``-based tests.
- ``specs/`` - Requirements, design, and task documentation.
- ``userguide/`` - Standards, conventions, and documentation.

Environment Setup
=================

When working in a Codex container:

.. code-block:: bash

   ./development/setup-agent-container

For local development:

.. code-block:: bash

   ./repository-setup/rehome-repository
   ./development/setup-environment

Running Tests
=============

Activate the virtual environment:

.. code-block:: bash

   source .venv/bin/activate

Run ``unittest`` tests:

.. code-block:: bash

   python -m unittest discover -s source/tests -p "test_*.py"

